        "section_type": "example",
        "id": 8,
        "title": "Example 3: Trigonometric Identities",
        "renderer": "manim",
        "narration": "Let's consider triangle ACB, which is right-angled at C. We are given that the hypotenuse AB is 29 units and side BC is 21 units. The angle ABC is denoted by theta. Our task is to determine the values of two expressions: first, cos-squared theta plus sin-squared theta, and second, cos-squared theta minus sin-squared theta. Before we can do anything, we need to find the length of the third side, AC. Since we have a right-angled triangle, we can use the Pythagorean theorem. AC will be the square root of the hypotenuse squared minus the other side squared. So, AC equals the square root of 29 squared minus 21 squared. 29 squared is 841, and 21 squared is 441. The difference is 400. The square root of 400 is 20. So, side AC is 20 units long. Now we have all three sides relative to angle theta: the Adjacent side BC is 21, the Opposite side AC is 20, and the Hypotenuse AB is 29. Let's find sin theta and cos theta. Sin theta is Opposite over Hypotenuse, which is 20/29. Cos theta is Adjacent over Hypotenuse, which is 21/29. Now for the first expression: cos-squared theta plus sin-squared theta. We substitute our values: (21/29) squared plus (20/29) squared. This becomes 441/841 plus 400/841. Adding them gives 841/841, which is exactly 1. This is a very important result in trigonometry known as a Pythagorean identity. For the second expression, cos-squared theta minus sin-squared theta, we substitute the same values: (21/29) squared minus (20/29) squared. This is 441/841 minus 400/841, which gives us 41 divided by 841.",
        "narration_segments": [
          {
            "id": 1,
            "text": "Let's consider triangle ACB, which is right-angled at C. We are given that the hypotenuse AB is 29 units and side BC is 21 units. The angle ABC is denoted by theta.",
            "duration": 12
          },
          {
            "id": 2,
            "text": "Our task is to determine the values of two expressions: first, cos-squared theta plus sin-squared theta, and second, cos-squared theta minus sin-squared theta.",
            "duration": 11
          },
          {
            "id": 3,
            "text": "Before we can do anything, we need to find the length of the third side, AC. Since we have a right-angled triangle, we can use the Pythagorean theorem.",
            "duration": 9
          },
          {
            "id": 4,
            "text": "AC will be the square root of the hypotenuse squared minus the other side squared. So, AC equals the square root of 29 squared minus 21 squared.",
            "duration": 10
          },
          {
            "id": 5,
            "text": "29 squared is 841, and 21 squared is 441. The difference is 400. The square root of 400 is 20. So, side AC is 20 units long.",
            "duration": 11
          },
          {
            "id": 6,
            "text": "Now we have all three sides relative to angle theta: the Adjacent side BC is 21, the Opposite side AC is 20, and the Hypotenuse AB is 29.",
            "duration": 10
          },
          {
            "id": 7,
            "text": "Let's find sin theta and cos theta. Sin theta is Opposite over Hypotenuse, which is 20/29. Cos theta is Adjacent over Hypotenuse, which is 21/29.",
            "duration": 11
          },
          {
            "id": 8,
            "text": "Now for the first expression: cos-squared theta plus sin-squared theta. We substitute our values: (21/29) squared plus (20/29) squared.",
            "duration": 10
          },
          {
            "id": 9,
            "text": "This becomes 441/841 plus 400/841. Adding them gives 841/841, which is exactly 1. This is a very important result in trigonometry known as a Pythagorean identity.",
            "duration": 13
          },
          {
            "id": 10,
            "text": "For the second expression, cos-squared theta minus sin-squared theta, we substitute the same values: (21/29) squared minus (20/29) squared. This is 441/841 minus 400/841, which gives us 41 divided by 841.",
