            "title": "The Primary Ratios",
            "mnemonic": "SOH CAH TOA - 'Some Old Horses Can Always Hear Their Owners Approaching'",
            "explanation": "The most famous mnemonic in trigonometry. It directly tells you the formula for the three main ratios: Sine is Opposite over Hypotenuse, Cosine is Adjacent over Hypotenuse, and Tangent is Opposite over Adjacent."
          },
          {
            "letter": "B",
            "title": "Reciprocal Pairs",
            "mnemonic": "Sine & Cosecant, Cosine & Secant, Tangent & Cotangent.",
            "explanation": "Remember that each primary ratio has a 'co-' partner, but they don't always match up. Sine's partner IS Cosecant. But Cosine's partner is the one WITHOUT a 'co-', Secant. Tangent and Cotangent are the easy pair to remember."
          },
          {
            "letter": "C",
            "title": "Pythagorean Theorem",
            "mnemonic": "a² + b² = c² - 'The two short sides squared and summed, match the longest side's outcome.'",
            "explanation": "In any right-angled triangle, the square of the hypotenuse (the long side, c) is equal to the sum of the squares of the other two sides (the legs, a and b). This is your key to finding a missing side when you know the other two."
          }
        ]
